# ============================================================================
# justintmccain.com — monorepo
# ============================================================================
# THIS REPO IS PUBLIC. Anything not excluded here is world-readable, and git
# history is permanent — a file committed once and deleted later is still in
# the history. Check this list before adding anything to the tree.

# --- Dependencies & build caches --------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo
tools/metadata-scrubber/dist/

# --- Generated site output ---------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare Pages runs the build (see docs/LAUNCH.md), so these are produced in
# CI rather than committed. Everything ELSE in site/ — fonts, images, the master
# film, css/, js/, _headers, favicons — is hand-authored source and IS tracked.
#
# Consequence worth knowing: a fresh clone has no index.html until you run
# `node build/build.mjs`. That is expected, not a broken checkout.
site/index.html
site/privacy.html
site/sitemap.xml
site/scrubber/

# --- Not for a public repo ---------------------------------------------------
# Internal planning docs and a personal document. None of these help anyone
# reading the code, and the resume is a document you want to hand out
# deliberately rather than have scraped from a repo.
Justin_T_McCain_Resume_2026.docx
PHASE-2-PROMPT.md
tools/vanish/Vanish_PRD.docx
tools/metadata-scrubber/metadata-scrubber-PRD.md

# Superseded v1 assets, including a 2.3 MB backup of the old master film. 17 MB
# of history nobody needs. NOTE: build/ASSET-LOG.md references
# site-v1-archive/signal-master-v1.mp4 — that path will not exist in a clone.
site-v1-archive/

# --- Local tooling -----------------------------------------------------------
# launch.json is genuinely useful to a contributor (it starts the preview
# server), so it stays. settings.local.json is a per-machine permission grant
# and is not.
**/.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing here uses env vars today. This is a guard against the day something
# does, not documentation that something exists.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- macOS -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Found inside site/ during a deploy pre-flight, where it was serving 200 at
# https://justintmccain.com/.DS_Store and leaking a directory listing. Finder
# recreates it on every folder view, so build.mjs also sweeps site/ on each
# build — belt and braces, because this one already got through once.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# --- Local scratch -----------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.bak.mp4
*.log
npm-debug.log*
